==Battleground==
*1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*15 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*2 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 70 seconds<sup>2,100f</sup>.
*10 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*2 [[Puffzerker]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 90 seconds<sup>2,700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 4.67~6.67 seconds<sup>140f~200f</sup>.
*3 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 56.67~60 seconds<sup>1,700f~1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Ange Lackey]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Heavenly Hippoe]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage does not put any real pressure on the player, so it will not be able to respond to an extremely aggressive strategy. Simply send out attackers of your choice like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and any [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rushers]] (especially [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]) and some defense with [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] and [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], and the difficult enemies should die before the aggressive push even reaches Dark Emperor Nyandam.

[[Master of Selection Darvin (Special Cat)|Darvin]] and [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]] form a strong synergy in this stage. Darvin protects Newtone from Nyandam, as well as any pushes from Shy Boy or Puffzerker while Newtone mitigates the pressure on Darvin by pushing enemies away with damage and CC.

Multiple stronger enemies do spawn later in the stage, but there is likely to be enough DPS on the field when they do that they will melt.

==Trivia==
*Smothering Scheme's Japanese name (好き好きスキーム) could mean "Love Love Scheme" or "Matter-of-Taste Scheme" depending on whether 好き好き is read as ''suki suki'' (好き, meaning "like" or "love", said twice) or ''sukizuki'' (matter of taste).

